de (moe-cache prefill, no admission) REJECTED: mechanism never engages (x86-main)\nClaim category: failed candidate (engine code) + methodology. Evidence: evidence/claude-code.jsonl task X4; artifacts/x4-shot/correct/{off,lru384,hot325,hot487}.{out,err}; image llamacpp-shot2 (run_ref sha256:7040afcd..., config sha256:8edec18d..., patch cc/moe_static_hot/static-hot.patch sha256 0d91a155...). Build record shot-2 status=failed at stage linkage (symbol tools unavailable in runtime image; ldd OK) — binaries otherwise identified (tools hashed, archive saved).\nSame binary, chat prompt, -n 160, -c 4096, temp 0, seed 1, -ngl 99 --n-cpu-moe 24 (UNTIMED: host load ~6 from a Codex CPU job, so speeds are indicative only):\n  off (no cache) 102 t/s, text sha 76dc9422 | LRU 384 161 t/s, text sha 950b46b1 (= all-GPU reference D022 m1_static_n0) | static 325 100 t/s, 76dc9422 | static 487 111 t/s, 76dc9422.\nInterpretation: static mode returns no slot map -> scheduler keeps MUL_MAT_ID on the CPU (weights host-resident); the copy-callback fallback only acts when the op is placed on the GPU (artifacts/codexO/moe-cache-map.md predicted \"cache acceleration not promised\"). Output identical to the CPU path, speed ≈ off: the prefilled banks are allocated but unused.\nMethod lessons (-> methodology CC):\n - Greedy-output fingerprint: at temp 0, CPU-computed and GPU-computed experts give different text for this model; text sha256 identifies which backend actually computed the experts. Cheap engagement check before spending a timing window.\n - \"Compiles + default path unchanged\" (T-O's verification) did not test that the new path engages; every candidate needs an engagement observation (counter, log, or fingerprint) as its first GPU test.\nNext: T-R (expert-granular hybrid split, CPU computes cold experts) is the remaining candidate for the untested quadrant.\n# D028 — KV-cache precision as a memory lever (protocol frozen before results)\nQuestion: at long context, how much GPU memory does KV quantization save on Granite mixE4K, at what quality and speed cost? KV/token f16 = 24 layers x 2 x 8 kv-heads x 64 x 2 B = 48 KiB -> 1.5 GiB at 32k ctx (> mixE4K weights 779 MiB).\nImage: llamacpp-b0 (unpatched 31288c9c6). Tests lab/tests/kv1.json: decode/prefill at -c 32768 with the 1560-token prose prompt (-n 96) for KV f16/q8_0/q4_0 with -fa on, plus f16 -fa off control; 3 alternating rounds; PPL wikitext -c 4096 --chunks 6 per KV type.\nAccept a KV type as \"same accuracy\" if PPL within +1% of f16 (-fa on) AND greedy text identical or (if not) KLD check pending; report GPU delta MiB (nvidia-smi), prefill & decode t/s medians. Classification: representation (KV) trade-off — not an engine code gain.\nRESULT (job job-787f02f737, 7/15 clean; host monitor clean):\n- Quantized KV (q8_0, q4_0; -fa on) ABORTS at model load: ggml-impl.h:330 hash-set \"fatal error\" (SIGSEGV 139), in our b0 build AND the upstream ghcr full-cuda image at the same commit, with fit on or off, at 4k and 32k ctx -> engine defect in llama.cpp 31288c9c6 for this model/config, not our build. Delegated root cause: T-KVB. KV precision lever UNTESTED, not \"rejected\".\n- Flash attention alone (f16 KV, -c 32768, 1560-token prompt): GPU delta 2762 MiB (-fa on) vs 3746 MiB (-fa off) = -984 MiB; decode 627.2 vs 570.2 t/s (+10%), prefill 7001 vs 5865 t/s (+19%); text differs (96310158 vs f28de009; FA changes reduction order). PPL -c 4096 f16 FA 7.5385 (no non-FA PPL run -> quality equivalence of FA not measured here).\nClassification: memory-fit + speed observation for an existing engine option; factory rule candidate: \"enable flash attention for long context (removes the O(ctx) KQ buffer)\". 3 samples (gen), 1 (ppl).\n# D029 — C1 q8_reuse ACCEPTED: first full-engine computation-preserving gain (+2.1% Q8_0 decode), x86-main\nProtocol D026 (frozen, commit 474be3b before results). Job job-34c09bec98 (image llamacpp-q8reuse2, run_ref sha256:bd78b473..., config 111ddae8...; patch 9943dee4...), same binary GGML_CUDA_Q8_REUSE=0 vs 1, 2 ABBA cycles, 36/36 clean, host monitor 38 samples no compiler, load 2.7-5.0.\nllama-bench tg128 median t/s [range]: Q8_0 OFF 791.3 [789-792] ON 807.6 [806-808] = +2.06% (criterion >= +2%: MET, ranges disjoint). mixE4K OFF 702.9 ON 715.4 = +1.78% (below 2% -> mixE4K track \"consistent but sub-threshold\").\nllama-completion decode (chat, 160 tok): Q8_0 758.4 -> 777.0 (+2.45%); mixE4K 677.6 -> 691.2 (+2.0%). Prefill unchanged within noise.\nCorrectness: CUDA test-backend-ops MUL_MAT 2445/2445 OK; greedy text sha identical base/OFF/ON (Q8_0 65894776, mixE4K 950b46b1); PPL identical (Q8_0 9.653, mixE4K 9.9806, -ub 1).\nClassification: full-engine code gain, computation-preserving, discrete RTX 5070 Ti, Granite, batch-1 decode. Small: it's a launch/redundancy cleanup (D011 predicted 3-4.5%). Not memory-reducing; stacks with every memory technique. Component CC: cc/q8_reuse (integration: env switch, CUDA mmvq path, applies to 31288c9c6).\n# D030 — T-R hybrid expert split REJECTED as implemented (slower than static layer offload at equal GPU MiB)\nProtocol D027 (+amendment 1). Job job-d1fb4e9879 (image llamacpp-hsplit1 run_ref sha256:6e91ace0...), same binary for all, 27/27 clean, 3 alternating rounds.\nDecode median t/s (GPU delta MiB): n18: static 149.8 (902) | static+flags 144.5 | split 125.3 (910) = -16%.  n12: 189.8 | 198.8 | split 160.8 (1072) = -19%.  n6: 309.1 | 311.5 | split 211.9 (1234) = -32%. Prefill also lower (split 211-252 vs static 269-322).\nQuality gate not reached (rejected on speed first); CUDA unit-test mismatch still open (amendment 1).\nKey observation: the deficit GROWS as more experts are hot (n18 -> n6), so CPU expert compute is not the bottleneck; candidates: (1) per-slot GPU dispatch (patch issues one MUL_MAT_ID per selected slot to avoid duplicate null IDs in mmid.cu -> up to 8x kernels per projection), (2) 24 GPU<->CPU handoffs/token (every layer has a cold part) vs K for static, (3) router-order GET_ROWS/transposes. Next discriminating experiment: nsys timeline split-n12 vs static-n12 (kernel count/token, sync count, CPU-busy intervals).\nLesson (methodology): single-layer harness predicted ~330 t/s at ~897 MiB (D019); the integrated graph pays per-layer fixed costs the harness did not model. Harness wins are hypotheses until integrated (prompt §13 confirmed).\n# D033 — Quantized KV fixed (T-KVB2 patch) and measured: q8_0 KV = same accuracy, -720 MiB at 32k\nFix: cc/kv_quant_fix/kv-quant-fix.patch sha256 dd0e4ffd... (Codex T-KVB2): the backend scheduler sizes its hash set for graph NODES only while storing nodes+leaves; quantized-KV extra ops push Granite's graph to 2065 tensors > 2053 slots -> GGML_ABORT. Generic capacity defect (upstream-worthy). Image kvfix-1 (Build CC success, run_ref sha256:7c31deda...).\nJob job-a945fa8656 (protocol D028 unchanged, 15/15 clean; download running concurrently: dl=3 in monitor, no compiler). -fa on, -c 32768, 1560-token prompt:\n  KV f16 2762 MiB, decode 625.1, prefill 7383 | q8_0 2042 MiB (-720), 559.2 (-10.5%), 6947 (-6%) | q4_0 1658 MiB (-1104), 502.3 (-20%), 7188 | f16 no-FA 3746 MiB, 573.7, 5916.\n  PPL wikitext -c 4096: f16 7.5385±0.171, q8_0 7.5392±0.171 (+0.01%: ACCEPT, same accuracy), q4_0 8.1368±0.185 (+7.9%: REJECT under the ±1% rule).\nFactory rules: long context -> -fa on (always); then KV q8_0 (needs kv_quant_fix on this llama.cpp pin) trades ~10% decode for ~26% less GPU KV+attention memory at ~equal PPL; q4_0 KV only with an explicit quality budget. Classification: representation (KV) trade-off + engine defect fix (the fix is a correctness enabler, not a speed gain).\n# D035 — Placement-aware precision (PAP) + imatrix: results (protocol D032-A), job job-3d2fbbd061 (48/48 clean)\nConditions: llamacpp-b0, chat -n 160 -c 4096, 3 alternating rounds; host monitor: no compiler, BUT the 18.6 GB proxy-2 download ran throughout (dl=3) and round 3 was slower for several configs -> decode spread 10-15% within a config (vs 1-